@base = http://localhost:8080

# Run reset.sql first, then the requests in order: ids and results depend on it.
# Every error answer (4xx/5xx) has the ApiError body:
# {"timestamp": "...", "status": 404, "error": "Not Found", "message": "...", "path": "..."}

########## GET /api/rooms — list, with optional filters ##########

### 1. List all rooms (200)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms

### 2. Filter by minimum capacity (200)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms?minCapacity=15

### 3. Filter by keyword in the name (200)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms?keyword=room

### 4. Both filters together (200)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms?minCapacity=15&keyword=room

### 5. Filters that match nothing — empty list (200)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms?minCapacity=15&keyword=nothing

### 6. minCapacity is not a number (400)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms?minCapacity=abc

########## GET /api/rooms/{id} — one room ##########

### 7. Get one room (200)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms/1

########## POST /api/rooms — create ##########

### 8. Create a room (201 + Location: /api/rooms/4)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Room C", "capacity": 8}

########## PUT /api/rooms/{id} — update ##########

### 9. Update the new room (200; one select, one update)
PUT {{base}}/api/rooms/4
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Room C (renamed)", "capacity": 12}

### 10. Update a room that does not exist (404)
PUT {{base}}/api/rooms/999
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Nope", "capacity": 10}

########## DELETE /api/rooms/{id} ##########

### 11. Delete the new room (204)
DELETE {{base}}/api/rooms/4

### 12. Delete a room that does not exist (404)
DELETE {{base}}/api/rooms/999

########## Validation and statistics ##########

### 13. Create with capacity 50 (400)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Too big", "capacity": 50}

### 14. Count rooms (200; Hibernate prints SELECT COUNT)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms/stats

########## Week 7 — reservations ##########

### 15. Reservations for room 1 (200, 3 items)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms/1/reservations

### 16. Reservations for a missing room (404)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms/99/reservations

### 17. Book room 1, Kim, 14 Oct 10–11 (201 + Location: /api/reservations/6)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms/1/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{"reservedBy": "Kim", "startTime": "2026-10-14T10:00:00", "endTime": "2026-10-14T11:00:00"}

### 18. Overlaps Mina, 6 Oct 10:30–11:30 (409)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms/1/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{"reservedBy": "Kim", "startTime": "2026-10-06T10:30:00", "endTime": "2026-10-06T11:30:00"}

### 19. Starts when Mina ends, 6 Oct 11:00–12:00 (201 + Location: /api/reservations/7)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms/1/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{"reservedBy": "Kim", "startTime": "2026-10-06T11:00:00", "endTime": "2026-10-06T12:00:00"}

### 20. End before start (400)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms/1/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{"reservedBy": "Kim", "startTime": "2026-10-06T12:00:00", "endTime": "2026-10-06T11:00:00"}

### 21. Book a missing room (404)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms/99/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{"reservedBy": "Kim", "startTime": "2026-10-06T12:00:00", "endTime": "2026-10-06T13:00:00"}

### 22. Reservations for one person (200, 2 items, one select)
GET {{base}}/api/reservations?reservedBy=Mina

### 23. Delete a room with reservations (409)
DELETE {{base}}/api/rooms/1

########## Assignment 5 — one reservation ##########

### 24. Get one reservation (200; the Location from 17 now opens)
GET {{base}}/api/reservations/6

### 25. Get a reservation that does not exist (404)
GET {{base}}/api/reservations/99

### 26. Cancel a reservation (204)
DELETE {{base}}/api/reservations/7

### 27. Cancel the same reservation again (404)
DELETE {{base}}/api/reservations/7

########## Lab E — PUT with dirty checking ##########

### 28. Get a room that does not exist (404)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms/99

### 29. Update room 2 (200; one select, then one update at commit — no save())
PUT {{base}}/api/rooms/2
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Study Pod", "capacity": 6}

### 30. Same body again (200; one select and NO update: nothing is dirty)
PUT {{base}}/api/rooms/2
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Study Pod", "capacity": 6}

### 31. Update with capacity 25 (400; no SQL at all)
PUT {{base}}/api/rooms/2
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Study Pod", "capacity": 25}

########## Lab E — every error has the ApiError body ##########

### 32. Id is not a number (400)
PUT {{base}}/api/rooms/abc
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Study Pod", "capacity": 6}

### 33. Create a room without a name (400)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{"capacity": 5}

### 34. Body is not valid JSON (400)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Broken", "capacity":

### 35. Search without reservedBy (400)
GET {{base}}/api/reservations

### 36. startTime is not a date (400)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms/1/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{"reservedBy": "Kim", "startTime": "tomorrow", "endTime": "2026-10-14T11:00:00"}

### 37. Book without reservedBy (400)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms/2/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{"startTime": "2026-10-20T10:00:00", "endTime": "2026-10-20T11:00:00"}

### 38. Overlaps Kim's booking from 17, 14 Oct 10:30–11:30 (409)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms/1/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{"reservedBy": "Lee", "startTime": "2026-10-14T10:30:00", "endTime": "2026-10-14T11:30:00"}

### 39. Delete room 2, which has reservations (409)
DELETE {{base}}/api/rooms/2

### 40. A URL with no endpoint (404)
GET {{base}}/api/nothing

### 41. Room 2 after 29–31 (200, capacity 6: 29 was saved without save(), 31 changed nothing)
GET {{base}}/api/rooms/2

########## My own failure requests ##########

### 42. Zero-length booking: start equals end (400)
POST {{base}}/api/rooms/3/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{"reservedBy": "Lee", "startTime": "2026-10-20T10:00:00", "endTime": "2026-10-20T10:00:00"}

### 43. Bad capacity on a missing room (400, not 404: the body is checked before the room is loaded)
PUT {{base}}/api/rooms/99
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Nope", "capacity": 0}
